title: 'Decided by Jeff: the command is ''skg-override-perspective'' on ''C-c v o''; it cycles, and each switch names the perspective it shows.'
pid: ccbab672-a083-407e-bf46-1de2a2dd97d1
body: |2-
  His words, under Top's message about the first switch: "rename that
  "C-c v o : skg-override-perspective"; let it cycle among every viewer
  whose view is in the buffer; name the reader's perspective in the
  minibuffer upon switching (you get minibuffer feedback in skg-for-ai,
  right?)". Neovim's is '<localleader>vo' (':SkgOverridePerspective');
  skg-for-ai's command was renamed 'override-perspective' to match, and
  prints "Perspective: NAME." as the clients' message does. 'C-c v p'
  is gone.
